WEBVTT

00:08.299 --> 00:09.718
[Jonathan] Nancy!

00:10.760 --> 00:12.303
[panting] Nancy!

00:12.387 --> 00:13.763
Come on, come on.

00:13.847 --> 00:15.432
Nancy!

00:17.559 --> 00:18.643
Where are you?

00:18.727 --> 00:21.771
[Nancy echoing] Jonathan! Jonathan!

00:22.355 --> 00:23.940
Jonathan!

00:25.650 --> 00:27.360
Jonathan, I'm right here!

00:28.028 --> 00:29.195
Nancy!

00:29.279 --> 00:31.531
[breathing heavily]

00:31.614 --> 00:32.741
Nancy!

00:33.616 --> 00:35.410
[Nancy] Jonathan, where are you?

00:35.493 --> 00:38.121
Jonathan! [breathing heavily]

00:38.204 --> 00:39.914
Jonathan!

00:39.998 --> 00:42.125
Jonathan, I'm right...
I'm right here!

00:42.208 --> 00:44.002
- [faintly] Where are you?
- [panting]

00:44.085 --> 00:45.712
- I'm right here!
- [Nancy] Jonathan!

00:45.795 --> 00:48.173
I'm right here! Nancy!

00:48.256 --> 00:52.469
- Just follow my voice!
- [panting] Jonathan!

00:52.552 --> 00:55.805
[Jonathan in distance]
Follow my voice, Nancy, I'm right here!

00:56.097 --> 00:57.182
Nancy!

00:57.265 --> 00:59.684
- [growling]
- [gasps]

01:00.226 --> 01:01.186
Nancy!

01:01.269 --> 01:03.229
[panting]

01:05.273 --> 01:07.275
- [growling continues]
- [breathing heavily]

01:11.071 --> 01:13.156
[squelching]

01:16.868 --> 01:18.578
[growling continues]

01:31.049 --> 01:32.092
Nancy?

01:34.552 --> 01:35.720
Nancy.

01:37.972 --> 01:40.850
[Jonathan in distance] Nancy!
Follow my voice!

01:42.602 --> 01:44.562
[monster growling]

01:46.523 --> 01:47.774
Nancy?

01:52.570 --> 01:54.531
[Jonathan gasps]

01:54.614 --> 01:56.282
- [Nancy] Jonathan!
- Nancy!

01:56.366 --> 01:59.452
- [Nancy straining]
- [Jonathan grunting]

02:09.379 --> 02:11.339
[Nancy sobbing]

02:11.422 --> 02:14.467
[Jonathan panting] I got you.

02:28.314 --> 02:30.316
[theme music playing]

03:30.793 --> 03:33.254
[pop song playing on car stereo]

03:37.008 --> 03:38.760
I just don't understand
why we're coming out here.

03:38.843 --> 03:42.096
- She obviously doesn't wanna talk to you.
- That's... that's not it.

03:42.180 --> 03:45.850
Oh, really? Because no girl
would ever blow off King Steve.

03:45.934 --> 03:48.603
She was acting weird.
I mean, something was wrong.

03:48.686 --> 03:50.605
So what? [scoffs]
Like, you're worried about her?

03:50.688 --> 03:54.108
- What?
- Aw, you are.

03:54.192 --> 03:56.903
- Aw, Steve has a heart.
- Would you just-- Stop.

03:56.986 --> 03:58.571
- Oh, Stevey's in love.
- Would you just shut up?

03:58.655 --> 03:59.989
- Who knew?
- Shut up!

04:00.073 --> 04:01.407
[chuckling] Jeez.

04:02.992 --> 04:05.411
- [Carol] Damn. Sorry.
- [Tommy chuckles]

04:10.375 --> 04:13.169
[sighs] So this is it, huh?
Princess' castle.

04:14.879 --> 04:16.923
[Steve] I'll just be a minute.

04:47.954 --> 04:49.372
[Joyce] Look, we gotta
go through this again.

04:49.455 --> 04:52.250
- I told you everything that I saw.
- Oh, gosh. Tell me again.

04:52.333 --> 04:54.627
- Upstairs or downstairs?
- Upstairs.

04:54.711 --> 04:55.837
There was a laboratory.

04:55.920 --> 04:58.506
It was where they must do experiments
or something, and then there was...

04:58.589 --> 04:59.632
[inhales deeply]

04:59.716 --> 05:01.134
There was this kid's room.

05:01.217 --> 05:04.887
- How do you know it was a kid's room?
- More like a prison.

05:04.971 --> 05:07.390
So why would you think
it was a kid's room, then?

05:07.473 --> 05:08.850
Because, I told you,

05:08.933 --> 05:11.644
the size of the bed, there was a drawing,
there was a stuffed animal--

05:11.728 --> 05:13.354
[stammers] You didn't say
there was a drawing.

05:13.438 --> 05:15.273
Yeah, there was a drawing of a...
an adult and a child.

05:15.356 --> 05:17.692
- It said "Eleven" on it.
- Was it good?

05:17.775 --> 05:20.028
It was a kid's drawing, Joyce.
It was stick figures.

05:20.111 --> 05:21.404
[sighs]

05:25.825 --> 05:27.785
Wasn't Will.

05:36.753 --> 05:37.962
Earl...

05:39.714 --> 05:40.840
The night that Benny died,

05:40.923 --> 05:46.220
Earl said he saw some kid
with a shaved head with Benny.

05:46.304 --> 05:50.058
Now, I pressed him,
he said it might be Will, but maybe...

05:50.141 --> 05:51.934
Wait... Maybe, it wasn't?

05:52.018 --> 05:54.354
Look... this woman, Terry Ives,

05:54.437 --> 05:56.522
she claims to have lost
her daughter, Jane.

05:56.606 --> 05:59.025
She sued Brenner,
she sued the government...

05:59.108 --> 06:01.486
Now, the claims came to nothing,
but what if...

06:03.237 --> 06:05.698
I mean,
what if this whole time I've been...

06:05.782 --> 06:07.450
I've been looking for Will...

06:08.451 --> 06:10.495
I've been chasing after some other kid?

06:16.667 --> 06:18.044
- [Jonathan gasps]
- [monster growling]

06:24.717 --> 06:26.302
- [growling]
- [gasps]

06:29.263 --> 06:30.264
[Jonathan] Nancy!

06:35.645 --> 06:36.729
[monster growls]

06:48.741 --> 06:50.243
Better?

06:52.078 --> 06:53.204
Yeah.

06:54.914 --> 06:58.084
Is this okay?
Uh, I found it in the closet.

07:00.086 --> 07:01.712
I can go home.
[stammers] I just figured--

07:01.796 --> 07:03.756
Yeah, no.
I... [stammers]

07:05.299 --> 07:08.136
- I don't wanna be alone.
- [sighs]

07:09.053 --> 07:12.265
- Do you?
- No. Uh... no.

07:13.683 --> 07:14.851
[sighs]

07:47.175 --> 07:49.177
Can you just come up here?

07:54.640 --> 07:55.766
Yeah.

08:07.445 --> 08:09.697
- Do you want the lights off, or--
- [softly] On.

08:10.907 --> 08:12.200
[softly] Yeah.

08:16.037 --> 08:17.413
You know, it...

08:18.414 --> 08:20.249
it can't get us in here.

08:25.588 --> 08:27.173
We don't know that.

09:32.071 --> 09:35.700
Uh, yeah, it's Ives.
Terry Ives. That's with a "Y."

09:35.783 --> 09:38.703
Yeah, I got a pen.
Hang on.

09:41.414 --> 09:42.665
Mmm-hmm.

09:43.916 --> 09:45.334
Mmm-hmm.

09:45.418 --> 09:48.546
Great, thanks.
I really appreciate this, Frank.

09:48.629 --> 09:50.631
Say hi to the boys for me, too, would you?

09:58.014 --> 09:59.682
Did you get it?

09:59.765 --> 10:01.684
- I got it.
- Okay.

10:14.322 --> 10:15.740
[grunting softly]

10:20.494 --> 10:22.496
[pages rustling]

10:22.580 --> 10:23.706
Oh...

10:24.707 --> 10:25.791
Hey.

10:27.168 --> 10:28.252
[Nancy] Hey.

10:29.128 --> 10:31.464
[grunts] Couldn't sleep?

10:35.301 --> 10:37.887
Every time I close my eyes, I just...

10:39.805 --> 10:42.516
keep seeing that... thing.

10:43.392 --> 10:47.063
Wherever I was, that place...

10:48.147 --> 10:50.733
I think that it lives there.

10:50.816 --> 10:52.652
It was feeding there.

10:53.986 --> 10:55.780
Feeding on that deer.

10:56.864 --> 10:59.241
That means that if...
[inhales deeply]

10:59.325 --> 11:01.744
if Will and Barbara...

11:05.665 --> 11:06.832
Hey.

11:07.458 --> 11:09.585
My mom said she talked to Will.

11:10.336 --> 11:13.005
If he's alive,
there's a chance Barbara is, too.

11:13.089 --> 11:15.091
That means that she's trapped...

11:15.716 --> 11:17.510
in that place.

11:21.472 --> 11:23.265
We have to find it again.

11:23.349 --> 11:25.309
You wanna go back out there?

11:25.851 --> 11:27.186
Maybe we don't have to.

11:27.853 --> 11:30.564
When I saw it,
it was feeding on that deer.

11:30.648 --> 11:33.776
- Meaning it's... it's a predator, right?
- Right.

11:33.859 --> 11:37.947
And it seems to hunt at night, like a...
a lion or a coyote.

11:38.030 --> 11:39.740
But it doesn't hunt in packs like them.

11:40.658 --> 11:42.993
It's always alone, like...

11:44.078 --> 11:45.121
like a bear.

11:45.204 --> 11:48.541
And remember at Steve's,
when Barb cut herself?

11:48.624 --> 11:52.169
- And then, last night, the deer...
- Hmm, it was bleeding, too.

11:52.294 --> 11:53.504
One sec.

11:54.463 --> 11:56.966
Sharks can detect blood
in one part per million.

11:57.049 --> 11:59.009
That's one drop of blood in a million,

11:59.093 --> 12:01.345
and they can smell it
from a quarter mile away.

12:01.429 --> 12:04.098
So you're saying it can detect blood?

12:05.599 --> 12:07.184
[softly] It's just a theory.

12:08.686 --> 12:10.187
We could test it.

12:12.523 --> 12:14.400
But if it works...

12:15.317 --> 12:17.278
At least we'll know it's coming.

12:18.279 --> 12:20.489
- [door knob rattles]
- [both gasp]

12:20.573 --> 12:23.075
- [Nancy sighs]
- [Karen] Honey, are you up?

12:23.159 --> 12:25.661
Yeah, I'm... I'm getting dressed.

12:25.745 --> 12:28.289
[Karen] I, uh, made
some blueberry pancakes.

12:28.372 --> 12:30.040
I'll be down in a second.

12:31.125 --> 12:32.626
- [footsteps receding]
- [sighing]

12:33.586 --> 12:34.962
[Jonathan sighing]

12:41.093 --> 12:43.554
- [sighs]
- Your mom doesn't knock?

12:43.637 --> 12:45.139
[both chuckle]

12:50.102 --> 12:51.437
[knocking on door]

12:57.026 --> 12:59.111
- Hi. Scott Clarke?
- Uh, yes.

12:59.195 --> 13:01.238
The same Scott Clarke
who teaches science and AV

13:01.322 --> 13:02.490
- at Hawkins Middle?
- The very same.

13:02.573 --> 13:03.824
Oh, wonderful.

13:03.908 --> 13:07.411
...and we're making a newsletter,
which we'll send out monthly.

13:07.495 --> 13:09.413
It'll showcase all the latest equipment,

13:09.497 --> 13:12.416
as well as how-to articles,
which the kids write themselves.

13:12.500 --> 13:13.918
Oh, that's neat.

13:14.001 --> 13:15.544
What we're really trying to do here,
Mr. Clarke--

13:15.628 --> 13:17.254
Uh, please, call me Scott.

13:17.379 --> 13:18.923
Scott.

13:19.006 --> 13:22.927
What we're trying to do here, Scott,
is to connect kids from all over the state

13:23.010 --> 13:25.012
and give them
the support and encouragement

13:25.095 --> 13:27.097
to pursue careers in technology.

13:27.181 --> 13:29.892
We feel these are the kinds of kids
that are going to make Indiana proud.

13:29.975 --> 13:32.520
I agree, yes.
Completely.

13:32.603 --> 13:35.606
So, you know any kids
you think might wanna participate?

13:35.689 --> 13:38.400
Oh, I have a few in mind.

13:49.078 --> 13:51.872
[Mike sighs] I just...
I can't believe she didn't come back.

13:51.956 --> 13:53.958
- [Dustin] She's gotta be close.
- She said it wasn't safe.

13:54.041 --> 13:56.585
She just messed up the compasses
because she wanted to protect us.

13:56.669 --> 13:58.796
- She didn't betray us.
- Mike, calm down.

13:58.879 --> 14:01.131
I shouldn't have yelled at her.
I never should've done that.

14:01.215 --> 14:03.801
- Mike, this isn't your fault.
- Yeah, it's Lucas'.

14:03.926 --> 14:05.010
It wasn't his fault, either.

14:06.428 --> 14:08.222
- It wasn't his fault?
- No.

14:08.305 --> 14:10.015
So you're saying
he wasn't way out of line?

14:10.099 --> 14:11.642
- Totally, but so were you!
- What?

14:11.725 --> 14:13.394
- And so was Eleven.
- Oh, give me a break!

14:13.477 --> 14:14.645
No, Mike, you give me a break!

14:14.728 --> 14:17.189
All three of you were being
a bunch of little assholes!

14:17.273 --> 14:18.816
I was the only reasonable one.

14:18.899 --> 14:21.569
But the bottom line is...
you pushed first.

14:21.652 --> 14:23.529
And you know the rule.
You draw first blood...

14:23.612 --> 14:25.364
No! No way!
I'm not shaking his hand.

14:25.447 --> 14:26.991
- You're shaking his hand!
- No, I'm not.

14:27.074 --> 14:30.119
This isn't a discussion.
This is the rule of law.

14:30.202 --> 14:33.998
Obey or be banished from the party.
Do you wanna be banished?

14:34.623 --> 14:35.958
- No.
- Good.

14:38.377 --> 14:39.545
Where are we going?

14:39.670 --> 14:41.964
Where do you think?
We're going to get Lucas.

14:42.047 --> 14:43.966
And then we're gonna find Eleven.

14:44.550 --> 14:45.885
[door opens]

14:46.802 --> 14:48.512
[breathing heavily]

14:59.940 --> 15:02.651
Today is a very special day.

15:04.194 --> 15:05.446
Do you know why?

15:08.407 --> 15:11.201
Because today, we make history.

15:12.244 --> 15:15.289
Today, we make contact.

15:16.415 --> 15:18.125
[breathing heavily]

15:21.378 --> 15:22.963
[birds chirping]

15:47.863 --> 15:49.239
[sighing]

15:54.411 --> 15:56.121
[breathing heavily]

15:59.416 --> 16:00.751
[screams]

16:02.628 --> 16:04.213
[birds chirping]

16:07.299 --> 16:08.968
[Karen] Here you go.

16:09.051 --> 16:11.095
Ah... yum.

16:12.012 --> 16:14.515
Okay.
Now, sweetie, swallow the pancake.

16:15.432 --> 16:17.643
Where is Nancy?
I thought she was coming down.

16:17.726 --> 16:19.937
[sighs] She is.

16:20.020 --> 16:23.065
Uh, she was.
I don't know.

16:23.148 --> 16:25.526
- Nancy, what's taking so long?
- [music playing faintly]

16:25.609 --> 16:27.236
Nancy?

16:27.319 --> 16:29.989
- [door knob rattles]
- [sighs] Nancy, come on.

16:31.156 --> 16:32.992
- [sighs]
- [music continues]

16:42.626 --> 16:44.128
Nan--

16:59.727 --> 17:01.270
[doorbell rings]

17:09.737 --> 17:11.155
What do you want?

17:15.743 --> 17:18.287
[sighs] I drew first blood, so...

17:33.343 --> 17:35.345
Okay, I'll shake.

17:36.055 --> 17:37.264
On one condition.

17:37.389 --> 17:39.433
We forget the weirdo
and go straight to the gate.

17:39.516 --> 17:40.934
- Then the deal's off.
- Fine!

17:41.018 --> 17:42.728
- Fine!
- [Dustin] No, no, not fine!

17:42.811 --> 17:44.104
Guys, seriously?

17:45.022 --> 17:47.441
Do you even remember
what happened on the Bloodstone Pass?

17:50.736 --> 17:54.364
[sighs] We couldn't agree on what path
to take, so we split up the party

17:54.448 --> 17:56.366
and those trolls took us out one by one.

17:56.450 --> 17:59.161
And it all went to shit.
And we were all disabled!

17:59.995 --> 18:02.122
So we stick together, no matter what!

18:02.206 --> 18:07.127
Yeah, I agree. But this is the party,
right here in this room.

18:07.211 --> 18:11.090
- El is one of us now.
- Um, no, she's not. Not even close!

18:11.215 --> 18:13.467
Never will be.
She's a liar, a traitor--

18:13.550 --> 18:15.344
She was just trying to keep us safe!

18:15.427 --> 18:16.970
She didn't mean to hurt you.
It was an accident!

18:17.054 --> 18:18.263
An accident?

18:18.347 --> 18:20.307
All right, accident or not...

18:20.390 --> 18:22.434
- admit it, it was a little awesome.
- Awesome?

18:22.518 --> 18:24.436
Yeah, she threw you in the air
with her mind!

18:24.561 --> 18:26.271
I could have been killed!

18:26.355 --> 18:29.149
Which is exactly why we need her.
She's a weapon!

18:29.233 --> 18:31.360
Do you seriously wanna fight
the Demogorgon with your wrist rocket?

18:31.443 --> 18:33.737
That's like R2-D2
going to fight Darth Vader.

18:33.821 --> 18:35.697
We're no use to Will if we're dead.

18:36.698 --> 18:39.910
If you two wanna waste your time
looking for a traitor, go ahead,

18:39.993 --> 18:43.247
'cause I'm not spending my time
on her anymore. No way!

18:44.748 --> 18:47.751
I'm going to the gate.
I'm gonna find Will.

19:06.645 --> 19:08.480
[upbeat music playing on PA]

19:14.486 --> 19:16.238
[indistinct chatter]

19:23.453 --> 19:24.496
[Dr. Brenner] It's okay, Eleven.

19:24.580 --> 19:28.041
Don't be frightened.
These are all friends.

19:29.543 --> 19:31.211
They're just here to watch.

19:33.297 --> 19:35.090
Don't focus on them.

19:35.174 --> 19:37.718
Stay in here, like before.

19:38.802 --> 19:40.387
Yes, Papa.

19:45.767 --> 19:48.854
Now, remember.
Whatever it is, it can't hurt you.

19:48.937 --> 19:52.524
Not from here.
So there's nothing to be frightened of.

19:54.318 --> 19:55.736
It's reaching out to you...

19:56.653 --> 19:58.655
'cause it wants you.

19:58.739 --> 20:00.365
Hmm?

20:00.449 --> 20:01.658
It's calling you...

20:02.576 --> 20:04.494
so don't turn away from it this time.

20:05.412 --> 20:06.914
I want you to find it.

20:07.831 --> 20:09.082
Understand?

20:10.000 --> 20:11.084
Yes.

20:45.744 --> 20:46.745
[man] Are you lost?

20:50.332 --> 20:51.541
Is your mom here?

20:54.044 --> 20:55.212
Your dad?

20:57.631 --> 20:59.174
Mouth breather.

21:10.852 --> 21:13.313
- What should we do?
- Uh...

21:15.190 --> 21:16.775
Call the police.

21:19.861 --> 21:23.824
Excuse me. Young lady!
You know you have to pay for those!

21:23.907 --> 21:25.617
- Hey! Stop right--
- [woman screams]

21:25.701 --> 21:27.119
- Please.
- [woman grunts]

21:27.202 --> 21:29.288
[stammers] You have to pay for those!

21:29.371 --> 21:31.873
Stop right there!
Thief! Thief!

21:32.874 --> 21:34.710
- [glass shattering]
- [clamoring]

21:58.442 --> 21:59.484
Can I help you?

21:59.568 --> 22:01.611
Hi, we're looking for Terry Ives.
Does she live here?

22:01.695 --> 22:04.656
- Who's asking?
- The Hawkins chief of police.

22:08.535 --> 22:11.371
And you want to talk to my sister?

22:11.455 --> 22:14.291
Well, if your sister's Terry Ives,
then, yeah, we do.

22:16.668 --> 22:17.961
Okay, well, you can come in,

22:18.045 --> 22:20.130
but if you want Terry
to tell you anything,

22:20.213 --> 22:22.299
you're about five years too late.

22:22.424 --> 22:24.801
[TV playing indistinctly]

22:24.885 --> 22:26.762
Terry, you have some visitors.

22:27.929 --> 22:31.391
Hello.
My name's Joyce Byers.

22:31.516 --> 22:34.519
Uh, this is Hopper.
We drove over from Hawkins.

22:34.686 --> 22:37.981
Um, you see, uh, my son...

22:38.065 --> 22:41.318
he's been missing for almost a week now,

22:41.443 --> 22:44.571
and, um, we were wondering
if we could talk to you

22:44.696 --> 22:46.281
about your daughter, Jane?

22:46.406 --> 22:50.369
If there's anything that you could tell us
about when she was taken...

22:51.370 --> 22:53.205
What was your relationship
with Dr. Brenner?

22:54.206 --> 22:55.499
You guys keep in touch?

22:58.126 --> 23:00.170
This is, uh... this is him.

23:00.253 --> 23:02.714
[stammering] This is Will.

23:02.798 --> 23:05.550
Uh, you may have seen him on...
on the news.

23:05.675 --> 23:07.928
- Uh...
- What's wrong with her?

23:08.011 --> 23:10.722
I told you, you're wasting your time.

23:47.008 --> 23:48.885
[Dustin] This is weird without Lucas.

23:48.969 --> 23:51.847
- He should've shaken my hand.
- He's just jealous.

23:52.472 --> 23:53.890
What are you talking about?

23:55.058 --> 23:58.562
[sighs] Sometimes, your total
obliviousness just blows my mind.

24:00.439 --> 24:02.441
He's your best friend, right?

24:02.524 --> 24:06.528
- Yeah... I mean, I don't know.
- It's fine. I get it.

24:06.611 --> 24:10.115
I didn't get here until the fourth grade.
He had the advantage of living next door.

24:10.198 --> 24:11.533
But none of that matters.

24:11.616 --> 24:14.286
What matters
is that he is your best friend.

24:14.369 --> 24:16.705
And then this girl shows up
and starts living in your basement,

24:16.788 --> 24:18.665
and all you ever want to do
is pay attention to her.

24:18.748 --> 24:21.251
- That's not true.
- Yes, it is. And you know it.

24:21.334 --> 24:23.879
And he knows it.
But no one ever says anything

24:23.962 --> 24:26.423
until you both start punching
and yelling at each other

24:26.506 --> 24:28.967
like goblins
with intelligence scores of zero.

24:29.092 --> 24:31.761
- Now everything's weird.
- He's not my best friend.

24:31.845 --> 24:35.515
- [chuckles] Yeah, right.
- [sighs] I mean, he is, but so are you.

24:35.599 --> 24:38.018
- And so is Will.
- Can't have more than one best friend.

24:38.101 --> 24:39.811
- Says who?
- Says logic.

24:39.895 --> 24:43.482
Well, I call bull on your logic,
because you're my best friend, too.

24:44.483 --> 24:45.525
Okay.

24:45.609 --> 24:47.652
[panting]

24:50.155 --> 24:51.156
Whoa.

24:51.239 --> 24:53.533
- [indistinct conversations]
- [Dustin] You don't think...

24:53.617 --> 24:56.036
[panting] Uh... definitely.

25:07.839 --> 25:09.799
[audience applauding on TV]

25:09.883 --> 25:11.218
[host on TV] Are you ready?

25:11.301 --> 25:14.054
[Becky] She was a part of some study
in college.

25:14.137 --> 25:16.515
- MK Ultra?
- Yeah, that's the one.

25:16.598 --> 25:20.352
[exhales] Was, uh, started in the '50s.

25:20.435 --> 25:21.853
By the time Terry got involved,

25:21.978 --> 25:25.148
it was supposed to be ramping down,
but the drugs just got crazier.

25:25.232 --> 25:26.775
Messed her up good.

25:26.900 --> 25:29.194
This was the CIA that ran this?

25:31.112 --> 25:34.950
You and Terry would've gotten along.
"The Man," with a big capital "M."

25:35.033 --> 25:36.451
[sighing] They'd pay... you know,

25:36.535 --> 25:39.496
a couple hundred bucks
to people like my sister,

25:39.621 --> 25:43.291
give 'em drugs, psychedelics.
LSD, mostly.

25:43.375 --> 25:47.128
And then they'd strip her naked
and put her in these isolation tanks.

25:47.212 --> 25:49.047
- Isolation tanks?
- [Becky] Yeah.

25:49.130 --> 25:51.174
These big bathtubs, basically,

25:51.258 --> 25:53.885
filled with salt water,
so you can float around in there.

25:53.969 --> 25:56.638
You lose any sense of, uh...

25:56.721 --> 26:00.517
sense and feel nothing, see nothing.

26:00.600 --> 26:03.895
They wanted to expand
the boundaries of the mind.

26:04.020 --> 26:05.355
Real hippie crap.

26:05.438 --> 26:08.024
I... I mean, it's not like they were
forcing her to do any of this stuff.

26:08.108 --> 26:09.359
The thing is, though, is that

26:09.442 --> 26:11.528
she didn't know
she was pregnant at the time.

26:11.611 --> 26:13.113
Jane.

26:14.239 --> 26:15.448
[sighs]

26:16.700 --> 26:18.994
Do you have any pictures of her?

26:21.788 --> 26:24.082
I don't think you guys understand.

26:25.000 --> 26:27.377
Terry miscarried in the third trimester.

26:32.632 --> 26:35.552
She keeps all of this up.
Been doing it for 12 years.

26:35.635 --> 26:36.678
[sighs]

26:37.679 --> 26:41.641
Terry, uh, pretends like Jane is real,

26:41.725 --> 26:44.519
- like she's gonna come home someday.
- [lullaby plays from mobile]

26:44.603 --> 26:49.065
Says she's special.
Born with "abilities."

26:50.442 --> 26:51.985
Abilities?

26:53.778 --> 26:54.863
[bones cracking]

26:54.946 --> 26:56.656
You read any Stephen King?

26:56.740 --> 26:58.408
- [hisses]
- [beeping]

26:59.409 --> 27:00.452
[stammers]

27:00.535 --> 27:01.870
[chuckles]

27:01.953 --> 27:04.289
You guys look scared, actually.

27:04.372 --> 27:07.208
[chuckles] I mean, it's all make-believe.

27:08.084 --> 27:10.128
[clears throat]
What... what kind of abilities?

27:10.211 --> 27:12.881
Telepathy, telekinesis...

27:13.006 --> 27:14.633
[Eleven screams]

27:14.716 --> 27:16.801
You know, shit you can do with your mind.

27:17.761 --> 27:20.847
That's why the big, bad Man
stole Jane away.

27:20.930 --> 27:22.390
[yelling] Papa!

27:22.474 --> 27:25.477
Her baby's a weapon,
off fighting the commies.

27:25.602 --> 27:29.731
You know, the doctors all say
it's a coping mechanism.

27:29.814 --> 27:31.524
You know, to deal with the guilt.

27:31.608 --> 27:34.569
Do you think there is any chance
she could be telling the truth?

27:35.695 --> 27:37.947
[stammering] About having had the kid.

27:38.031 --> 27:40.825
There is no birth certificate,
nothing from the hospital.

27:40.909 --> 27:43.995
Doctors and nurses
all confirm that she miscarried.

27:44.079 --> 27:47.248
Yeah, but that could've been covered up.
Right?

27:47.957 --> 27:51.252
Like I said, you and Terry
would've gotten along.

28:13.274 --> 28:15.360
Oh, man.

28:15.443 --> 28:16.903
[grunts]

28:29.040 --> 28:30.375
[clattering]

29:04.993 --> 29:08.079
And I'll have four boxes of the .38s.

29:15.462 --> 29:17.922
What you kids doin' with all this?

29:18.089 --> 29:19.424
Um...

29:22.260 --> 29:25.221
- Monster hunting.
- Huh. [scoffs]

29:25.388 --> 29:26.514
[cash register dings]

29:28.433 --> 29:29.684
"Monster hunting"?

29:32.562 --> 29:34.063
You know, last week...

29:34.689 --> 29:37.984
I was shopping for a new top
I thought Steve might like.

29:38.067 --> 29:39.903
It took me and Barb all weekend.

29:39.986 --> 29:43.865
It seemed like life or death, you know?
And... and now--

29:43.948 --> 29:46.493
You're shopping for bear traps
with Jonathan Byers.

29:47.410 --> 29:48.536
Yeah.

29:49.746 --> 29:51.039
What's the weirdest part?

29:51.956 --> 29:53.374
Me or the bear trap?

29:54.292 --> 29:56.628
You.
It's definitely you.

29:56.711 --> 29:58.087
[chuckles]

29:58.171 --> 29:59.923
- [car horn honking]
- [Reed] Hey, Nance!

30:00.799 --> 30:03.510
Can't wait to see your movie. [laughs]

30:03.593 --> 30:04.969
What the hell was that?

30:06.429 --> 30:07.764
I don't know.

30:11.392 --> 30:12.519
What?

30:15.104 --> 30:16.731
What?

30:16.856 --> 30:18.441
Hey! Where are you going?

30:19.192 --> 30:22.737
- [panting]
- Nancy, wait!

30:24.113 --> 30:25.156
[whimpers]

30:26.449 --> 30:27.617
Nancy!

30:34.791 --> 30:37.210
[man 1] I can't believe it.
[man 2] These kids!

30:38.253 --> 30:39.587
- [Jonathan] Jesus.
- [sighs]

30:42.715 --> 30:44.050
Wow.

30:46.553 --> 30:49.222
- [spray can hissing]
- [Tommy laughing]

30:49.305 --> 30:50.348
[Jonathan] Wait!

30:50.431 --> 30:52.016
[Carol] Tommy,
you write like a three-year-old.

30:52.100 --> 30:54.060
[Tommy] Shut up!
[Nicole] I didn't know you could spell.

30:54.143 --> 30:55.144
[Tommy speaks indistinctly]

30:56.312 --> 30:58.731
[indistinct chatter]

30:58.815 --> 31:00.024
[laughter]

31:01.234 --> 31:03.111
Aw, hey there, princess!

31:03.903 --> 31:05.780
[Tommy] Uh-oh! She looks upset.

31:08.241 --> 31:09.325
[Carol] Oh!
[Tommy] Damn!

31:09.409 --> 31:10.743
What is wrong with you?

31:10.827 --> 31:12.120
What's wrong with me?
What's wrong with you?

31:12.203 --> 31:13.746
I was worried about you.

31:13.830 --> 31:15.915
I can't believe that I was
actually worried about you. [scoffs]

31:15.999 --> 31:19.252
- What are you talking about?
- I wouldn't lie if I were you.

31:19.335 --> 31:22.463
You don't want to be known
as the lying slut now, do you?

31:22.547 --> 31:23.756
Speak of the devil.

31:25.049 --> 31:26.092
Hi.

31:27.760 --> 31:28.928
You came by last night?

31:29.470 --> 31:32.557
Ding! Ding! Ding!
Does she get a prize?

31:32.640 --> 31:35.393
Look, I don't know what you think you saw,
but it wasn't like that.

31:35.476 --> 31:38.855
What, you just let him into your room
to... study?

31:38.938 --> 31:41.524
Or for another
pervy photo session? [laughs]

31:41.608 --> 31:43.151
- We were just--
- [Steve] You were just what?

31:43.234 --> 31:44.819
Finish that sentence.

31:46.946 --> 31:49.782
Finish the sentence.

31:50.658 --> 31:52.577
[breathing heavily]

31:56.372 --> 31:58.291
[scoffs] Go to hell, Nancy.

31:59.042 --> 32:00.501
Come on, Nancy, let's just leave.

32:00.585 --> 32:02.128
You know what, Byers?
I'm actually kind of impressed.

32:02.211 --> 32:03.713
I always took you for a queer,
but I guess you're just

32:03.838 --> 32:05.840
a little screw-up like your father.

32:05.924 --> 32:08.593
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
Yeah, that house is full of screw-ups.

32:08.676 --> 32:10.178
You know, I guess I shouldn't
really be surprised.

32:10.261 --> 32:11.471
A bunch of screw-ups in your family.

32:11.554 --> 32:12.722
- Jonathan, leave it.
- I mean, your mom...

32:12.805 --> 32:14.641
I'm not even surprised
what happened to your brother.

32:14.724 --> 32:15.767
[Nancy] Steve, shut up!

32:15.850 --> 32:16.851
I'm sorry I have to be
the one to tell you,

32:16.935 --> 32:18.728
but the Byers, their family,
it's a disgrace to the entire--

32:18.811 --> 32:19.854
[grunts]

32:19.979 --> 32:22.148
- [groans]
- [Jonathan breathing heavily]

32:22.690 --> 32:24.275
- [grunts]
- [Nancy] Steve!

32:24.359 --> 32:26.027
- [Tommy] Oh!
- [both grunting]

32:26.110 --> 32:27.695
- [Nancy] Steve.
- [groans]

32:28.613 --> 32:30.531
Stop! Steve!
Knock it off, you guys!

32:30.615 --> 32:32.700
- [Carol] Get off of him, seriously!
- Kick his ass, man!

32:32.784 --> 32:34.160
- [Carol] Get off! Stop!
- [both continue grunting]

32:35.912 --> 32:37.497
- Get in there, he's going to hurt himself!
- Easy, easy!

32:37.580 --> 32:40.333
Hey. Hey! Get out of here!
Get out of here! Get out of here!

32:41.542 --> 32:43.419
[both grunting]

32:44.295 --> 32:46.756
Jonathan, stop!
Stop! You're going to hurt him!

32:46.839 --> 32:48.800
- Jonathan, stop!
- [sirens wailing]

32:48.883 --> 32:51.010
[Tommy] Cops!
[Nancy] Guys-- Jonathan, get off of him!

32:51.094 --> 32:53.262
- Stop it!
- [Tommy] Cops! Come on!

32:53.346 --> 32:55.264
- Stop it! Come on!
- Cops!

32:55.348 --> 32:57.517
- You have to stop!
- Just go, Carol!

32:57.600 --> 32:59.060
- [Nancy] Stop it!
- [both grunting]

32:59.143 --> 33:00.770
Hey, he's had enough, man!
I said he's had enough!

33:00.895 --> 33:02.647
- Kids! All right!
- Stop it!

33:02.730 --> 33:04.065
[indistinct clamoring]

33:04.148 --> 33:05.733
[Callahan] Oh! My nose!

33:05.817 --> 33:07.610
[Powell] Calm him down!

33:07.694 --> 33:10.279
- [grunting]
- Go, go, go, go, go, go!

33:10.363 --> 33:14.242
Hey! Hey, uh-uh. Uh-uh.
Come here, little guys! Come here!

33:14.325 --> 33:15.910
- [Jonathan] Get off!
- I got this one!

33:15.994 --> 33:18.913
[Callahan] Get back here!
Get back here, you little punks!

33:21.290 --> 33:22.834
[breathing heavily]

33:22.917 --> 33:25.461
[audience cheering on TV]

33:25.545 --> 33:27.922
[man on TV]
Good gift for a college student...

33:28.006 --> 33:29.424
[continues indistinctly]

33:34.303 --> 33:36.055
[Hopper] Well, thank you for your time.
We appreciate it.

33:36.139 --> 33:38.266
[Becky] Hmm, yeah,
I'm sorry I couldn't be of more help.

33:40.059 --> 33:41.060
[door opens]

33:41.144 --> 33:43.479
- Good luck.
- [Hopper] Thank you.

33:48.151 --> 33:49.652
[sighing]

33:51.195 --> 33:52.280
Hey...

33:53.364 --> 33:54.907
[softly] What?

33:55.575 --> 33:57.035
We're gonna find him.

33:59.162 --> 34:02.248
Yeah, like Terry found her daughter?

34:03.708 --> 34:05.126
We're close.

34:05.209 --> 34:10.173
[breath trembling] Twelve years?
Twelve years she's been looking for her--

34:10.298 --> 34:11.966
And then she shows up
at Benny's five nights ago,

34:12.050 --> 34:13.259
which means we've got a chance.

34:13.342 --> 34:15.053
You know what I would give?

34:16.095 --> 34:18.347
For a chance?

34:18.431 --> 34:20.141
You know what I would give?

34:21.059 --> 34:22.560
[Callahan over radio]
Hey, Chief, you there?

34:22.685 --> 34:24.854
- Hey, Chief?
- Yeah, go ahead.

34:24.979 --> 34:26.731
Yeah, a fight broke out here and--

34:26.814 --> 34:30.026
- Cal, I don't have time for this.
- It's Jonathan Byers.

34:30.109 --> 34:32.153
You haven't seen Joyce, have you?

34:44.665 --> 34:46.959
Do you think we'll be out of here soon?

34:47.043 --> 34:49.170
You, yes. Him, no.

34:49.253 --> 34:51.464
He assaulted a police officer.

34:51.589 --> 34:53.841
- [ice cubes clatter]
- Well, how long are you gonna keep him?

34:53.925 --> 34:56.094
You and your boyfriend
have big plans, do you?

34:56.177 --> 34:58.387
[chuckles] He's not my boyfriend.

34:58.471 --> 35:00.973
I think you better tell him that.

35:01.682 --> 35:02.725
What?

35:02.809 --> 35:05.561
Only love makes you that crazy,
sweetheart.

35:06.604 --> 35:08.481
And that damn stupid.

35:09.398 --> 35:10.608
[sighs]

35:16.989 --> 35:18.324
Found some ice.

35:20.701 --> 35:21.869
Thanks.

35:24.455 --> 35:25.581
[sniffs]

35:30.169 --> 35:31.337
[sighs]

35:35.591 --> 35:36.926
Everything okay?

35:38.678 --> 35:39.804
Yeah.

35:40.930 --> 35:42.515
Everything's fine.

35:45.518 --> 35:46.686
[sighs]

35:55.611 --> 35:57.446
[Dustin shouting in the distance] El!

35:59.615 --> 36:01.367
[Mike shouting] Eleven!

36:03.911 --> 36:06.706
- Eleven! El!
- El!

36:07.999 --> 36:09.584
Eleven!

36:09.667 --> 36:10.877
Eleven!

36:12.628 --> 36:13.754
[panting]

36:13.921 --> 36:16.799
- Hey, stop. Do you hear that?
- What?

36:16.883 --> 36:17.967
El!

36:18.968 --> 36:20.011
El?

36:24.515 --> 36:25.808
Hey, there, Frogface.

36:26.726 --> 36:27.768
Toothless.

36:27.852 --> 36:29.729
Shit! Run, Mike!

36:29.812 --> 36:31.856
- What?
- Run! Come on!

36:32.690 --> 36:34.108
[Troy] You're dead, Wheeler.

36:34.192 --> 36:35.902
[Dustin] Move, Mike!

36:35.985 --> 36:37.570
Mike, come on, run!

36:45.786 --> 36:47.496
[beeping]

36:50.833 --> 36:52.793
[beeping continues]

37:04.722 --> 37:06.182
[beeping intensifies]

37:46.097 --> 37:49.684
[breathing heavily]

37:52.979 --> 37:54.689
[panting]

37:54.772 --> 37:56.732
[groans] Cramp!

37:56.816 --> 37:58.484
- Just keep going!
- [grunts]

37:58.567 --> 37:59.735
Keep going!

38:05.866 --> 38:07.326
Shit!

38:09.036 --> 38:11.205
- Stay back!
- Don't come any closer!

38:13.791 --> 38:16.419
- [grunts]
- [scoffs] Nice throw, numbnuts.

38:16.502 --> 38:18.212
[yelling]

38:18.337 --> 38:19.672
[grunting]

38:19.755 --> 38:21.424
- [gasps]
- Get off! Get off me!

38:21.507 --> 38:23.384
Let him go! Let him go!

38:23.467 --> 38:26.429
- Stay back, or I cut him!
- What do you want?

38:26.512 --> 38:27.722
I want to know how you did it!

38:27.805 --> 38:29.098
- How I did what?
- [Dustin whimpers]

38:29.181 --> 38:30.474
I know you did something to me.

38:30.558 --> 38:32.435
Some nerdy science shit
to make me do that.

38:32.601 --> 38:33.811
You mean piss your pants?

38:34.895 --> 38:36.480
Our friend has superpowers,

38:36.564 --> 38:38.983
and she squeezed your tiny bladder
with her mind.

38:39.066 --> 38:40.443
- Shut up!
- [groaning]

38:40.526 --> 38:42.862
I think I should save Toothless here
a trip to the dentist.

38:42.945 --> 38:44.655
Help him lose the rest of his baby teeth.

38:44.739 --> 38:46.574
Let him go.
Let him go!

38:46.657 --> 38:48.868
I'll let him go, sure.

38:48.951 --> 38:51.245
- But first... it's your turn.
- [panting]

38:51.329 --> 38:52.455
My turn for what?

38:52.538 --> 38:54.165
Wet yourself.

38:54.999 --> 38:57.001
- What?
- Jump...

38:57.084 --> 38:59.545
or Toothless here
gets an early trip to the dentist.

38:59.628 --> 39:00.921
[Dustin] Stop! No!

39:01.547 --> 39:02.923
[gasping]

39:05.551 --> 39:06.719
I'll cut him right now!

39:07.970 --> 39:09.138
[whimpering]

39:09.221 --> 39:11.682
All right, just hold on!
Hold on!

39:11.766 --> 39:14.101
Mike, don't do it.
I don't need my baby teeth, Mike!

39:14.226 --> 39:16.103
Mike, seriously, don't!

39:16.187 --> 39:18.439
[breathing heavily]

39:34.372 --> 39:35.873
[Dustin] Mike, don't do it!

39:35.956 --> 39:38.793
Seriously, don't do it, man!
Seriously, don't!

39:38.876 --> 39:40.753
Troy, I don't think
this is a good idea, man.

39:41.629 --> 39:43.172
[Dustin] Mike, don't!

39:43.255 --> 39:46.884
- Dentist's office opens in five...
- [Dustin panting]

39:46.967 --> 39:49.387
Four! Three!

39:51.138 --> 39:53.265
- Two!
- Mike!

39:53.349 --> 39:54.350
[Troy] One!

39:55.643 --> 39:57.103
- [Mike screams]
- [gasps]

40:03.901 --> 40:05.111
Holy shit.

40:05.194 --> 40:06.487
[Mike gasping]

40:15.329 --> 40:18.249
[whimpering]
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

40:27.341 --> 40:28.426
[grunts]

40:44.650 --> 40:46.402
- [bone cracks]
- [screaming]

40:46.485 --> 40:48.863
[Troy] She broke my arm! My arm!

40:48.946 --> 40:49.989
Go.

40:51.198 --> 40:53.909
[Troy] Let's get out of here! Let's go!
[James] Go!

40:53.993 --> 40:55.911
Yeah, that's right!
You better run!

40:56.662 --> 40:59.123
She's our friend and she's crazy!

40:59.206 --> 41:01.584
You come back here and she'll kill you!

41:01.667 --> 41:05.588
You hear me?
She'll kill you, you sons of bitches!

41:05.671 --> 41:07.715
[echoing] She'll kill you, you hear me?

41:08.841 --> 41:10.843
[ticking]

41:12.303 --> 41:14.221
[breathing heavily]

41:17.725 --> 41:19.351
[water trickling]

41:26.108 --> 41:27.860
[monster growling]

41:47.254 --> 41:49.006
[growling]

42:05.814 --> 42:09.568
- [roars]
- [screaming]

42:13.197 --> 42:14.573
[loud banging]

42:16.492 --> 42:18.452
[people clamoring]

42:23.832 --> 42:25.167
[Mike] El, are you okay?

42:25.251 --> 42:26.835
El?

42:27.878 --> 42:30.631
[sobbing] Mike... I'm sorry.

42:30.756 --> 42:33.217
Sorry? What are you sorry for?

42:34.260 --> 42:35.678
The gate...

42:39.557 --> 42:40.975
I opened it.

42:44.645 --> 42:46.063
I'm the monster.

42:47.481 --> 42:50.150
No. No, El, you're not the monster.

42:50.234 --> 42:51.819
You saved me.

42:51.902 --> 42:54.780
Do you understand?
You saved me.

43:34.612 --> 43:38.282
I have eyes on 'em now.
They're heading home.

43:48.584 --> 43:50.210
[engine starting]

44:23.786 --> 44:25.788
[theme music playing]
